{"findings":[
{"rule":"H1","where":"Deployment._configureModules (calls compliance.removeModule(maxBalanceModule) after super)","severity":"HIGH","why":"The override unbinds MaxBalanceModule right after the cap is set, so ModularCompliance.canTransfer no longer calls it. No holding limit applies to mint, transfer, transferFrom or batchTransfer.","steps":"Setup runs. Agent calls token.mint(b, 5000), which passes because only CountryRestrictModule is checked. The same happens with transfer(b, amount) for any amount."}
,
{"rule":"H2","where":"Deployment._configureModules (removeModule of MaxBalanceModule)","severity":"HIGH","why":"With the module unbound, no per-identity cap exists. Wallets a1 and a2, which share identity idA, can together hold far more than 1000.","steps":"Agent mints 1000 to a1 and then 1000 to a2. Both succeed and idA holds 2000."}
,
{"rule":"H3","where":"Deployment._configureModules / ModularCompliance.transferred, created, destroyed","severity":"MEDIUM","why":"The unbound module no longer receives moduleMintAction, moduleTransferAction or moduleBurnAction. Its _IDBalance records stay at 0 while real balances change, so the records do not match the token balances.","steps":"Agent mints 500 to b. Then call maxBalanceModule.getIDBalance(compliance, idB), which returns 0 while token.balanceOf(b) is 500."}
]}
